BEFORE WE GET TO LEVEL 4, we need to understand that the goal of level 1, 2 and 3
is to move data, they dont care about data arriving correctly and intact

level 4: provies reliable data delivery, flow control, and error correction


==>     level 4: the transport layer

layer 3 is about explain how to get a packet to its correct destintion
layer 4 is about data getting delivered reliably

the network layer is connectionless, it just sends data and hopes it arrives
theres no guqrteened packets will arrive in order or even arrive at all
this a problem that layer 4 solves!


==> sending a packet over the internet isnt enought!
==> we need reliability!
==> this layer is responsible for end to end communication, meaning reliability! making sure your data actually arives intact!

==> this is where TCP and UDP live

1- TCP:
TCP is what the web is built on
load a web page
download anything over the internet
send an email

--> before sending data
TCP establishes a connection between your computer and the server
this is called the three way handshake

a- your computer sayas, i want to connect
b- the server says "okay im ready"
c- your computer says great, lets go


only then does the data transmition begins

==> 
TCP breaks your data into segements
each segment gets a sequence number
so the receiving computers knows what order to reassemble them in
--> as segments arrive, the receviers sends back the the order in which it receives the segments
 kinda says: i got segment 1, s2, s3

 if a segment doesnt arrive, or it arrives corrupted, the receiver doesnt send an aknolegment
the sender automatically retransmist that missing/corrupted segment

thats reliability


2- UDP:
UDP just fires the data out without establishing a connection
without checkign if it arrive, or the order
UDP is useful for its speed
useful for video streaming, gaming, voice calls
few dropped packets dont matter, you want to keep playing, watchign or calling

in this layer, you need to be aware of the port numbers
so in this layer (transport layer) can identify the specific application
ports let multiple application use the same computer without interfering with each otehr

the transport layer also handles flow control:
    1- if the sender sends data faster than the receiver can handle
    the receviers tells the sender to slow the fuck down 
    this prevents overwhelming slower devices

    2- it also handles congestion control
    detecting when the internet if overloaded and reducing the tramsission speed to prevent making it worse





